# Where the dynamic loader looks for a DT_NEEDED library, for the packages that
# put their private libraries outside the default directories.
#
# musl reads this file and uses it INSTEAD of its built-in default, so the
# ordinary directories have to be listed here too. Samba is the reason it
# exists: its libraries name each other with no DT_RUNPATH at all, so
# libsamba-modules-samba4.so cannot find libsamba-debug-samba4.so unless
# /usr/lib/samba is searched. Chromium keeps its own libraries beside itself
# for the same reason.
/lib
/usr/lib
/usr/local/lib
/usr/lib/samba
/usr/lib/chromium
